# Window: the client response path, after the transaction has committed.
#   ClientInterface hands each InitiateResponseMessage to the connection's
#   network thread as a ClientResponseWork; getSerializedSize removes the
#   client handle and readies the response for the wire.
#
# Fault: hold every 25th response on its network thread for 1.5 s, longer
#   than the Jepsen client's 1 s procedure-call timeout, so the client gives
#   up on a transaction that did commit (an :info op). The network thread
#   also carries other connections' responses, which wait behind it.
#
# Correct behaviour: the delayed transactions are applied once, whether or
#   not their client saw the response; the workload checker finds no lost or
#   duplicated writes, and no node crashes.

RULE client-response-delay
CLASS org.voltdb.ClientInterface$ClientResponseWork
METHOD getSerializedSize
AT ENTRY
IF incrementCounter("client-response-delay") % 25 == 0
DO traceln("BYTEMAN client-response-delay fired");
   delay(1500)
ENDRULE
